description:
The final project: the server of a small multi-user workspace chat, as it would run behind a named pipe or loopback socket, with every concern of the course in it: a handshake with a version, validation of everything a client sends, rate limiting, events to other clients, clean handling of clients that quit or vanish. The transport is left out: the server receives one text line at a time from a client and returns the lines to send, and to whom.

```cpp
struct Out { int client; std::string line; };

class ChatServer
{
public:
    int connect();
    std::vector<Out> receive(int client, const std::string& line, std::uint64_t nowMs);
    std::vector<Out> disconnect(int client);
    std::vector<std::string> users() const;
};
```

**connect** registers a new connection and returns its id (1, 2, 3, ...). A client starts **not joined**.

**receive** handles one line. First, for any line from an open connection:
- more than 512 characters: reply `ERROR line too long`;
- **rate limit**: if this client has already sent 5 lines in the last 1000 ms (lines at times greater than `now - 1000`), reply `ERROR slow down` and do nothing else. Every line received counts, including refused ones.

Then the command is the text up to the first space; the rest (after that one space) is its argument:

| Line | Before joining | After joining |
|---|---|---|
| `HELLO 1 name` | join (below) | `ERROR already joined` |
| `SAY text` | `ERROR say hello first` | others get `FROM name text`; empty text: `ERROR empty message`; text over 200 characters: `ERROR message too long` |
| `TELL name text` | `ERROR say hello first` | that user gets `PRIVATE sender text`; unknown user: `ERROR no such user name`; missing text: `ERROR usage: TELL name text` |
| `WHO` | `ERROR say hello first` | `USERS a,b,c` (all joined names) |
| `QUIT` | `BYE`, connection closed | `BYE`, others get `LEFT name`, connection closed |
| anything else | `ERROR unknown command X` | `ERROR unknown command X` |

**Joining** with `HELLO version name`: a version other than `1` gets `ERROR unsupported version` and the connection is **closed**. A name must be 1 to 16 characters of letters, digits, `_` and `-` (`ERROR bad name`) and not already used, ignoring case (`ERROR name taken`). On success the client gets `WELCOME name` and every other joined client gets `JOINED name`.

Replies to the sender come first, then messages to others in client id order. "Others" means joined clients other than the sender. Names in `USERS` and **users** are sorted ignoring case. A closed or unknown connection: `receive` and `disconnect` return nothing.

**disconnect** is a connection that vanished: if the client had joined, the others get `LEFT name`.

